# Detection 012 – Privileged Group Membership Changes

## 1. Overview

Windows records security-enabled group membership changes through specific Security Event IDs.

Attackers may add compromised accounts to privileged groups to gain elevated access and maintain persistence.

## 2. Objective

Monitor changes to security-enabled groups and identify unauthorized additions to privileged groups.

## 3. Windows Event Information

| Event ID | Description |
|---|---|
| 4728 | Member added to a security-enabled global group |
| 4732 | Member added to a security-enabled local group |
| 4756 | Member added to a security-enabled universal group |

## 4. Detection Query – Identify Group Membership Changes

```spl
index=YOUR_INDEX sourcetype="YOUR_WINDOWS_SECURITY_SOURCETYPE"
(EventCode=4728 OR EventCode=4732 OR EventCode=4756)
| table _time host SubjectUserName MemberName TargetUserName
        Group_Name Group_Domain
| sort - _time
